   <h3> Voness</h3>
   <p>
   
Member since: Fri Mar 31, 2000<br>
was last logged in: Sat Apr  7, 2001 at 14:51



<p><b>Full name:</b> Voness Dyr'Fate


<br><b>Profile:</b>
Level 56 Male Teir Dal Rogue


<br><b>Religion:</b>
Innoruuk

<br><b>Hord Rank:</b>
Circle of Bones



<p><b>Voness's Bio:</b>
<table border=1 width=400>
  <tr><td>
  I grew up in the streets of Neriak. My Father and Mother captured and hung by the Halflings that have invaded Nektulos Forest. I was small and skinny compared to other males my age but, my wits, feet and hands were all faster than those I compared myself to. They bullied and pushed me around, when they could catch me. I was not welcome at the guild halls of the Indigo Brotherhood, so I have to find my livelyhood elsewhere. I took advantage of the deftness of my hands, and the fleetness of my feet. Ventures into the Foreign Quarter were prosperous. A handful of coins here, a piece of jewelry there, and the occasional small blade kept me fed through those roughest of times. I dared not practice my trade outside of the Foriegn Quarter. For if I had been caught pilfering from the Tier'Dal, I would have been slayed in the streets, and trod upon by passers by.

One day, I was observed in the act of "obtaining" some needed coin from an unattended cash box. As I fled with my loot, a shadow materialized from a nearby wall, and caught me by the hair. I thought I was dead for sure. The one who accosted me drug me from the Foreign Quarter, through the Neriak Commons and into the Third Gate. All I could make out of him was a shadowy form. When we entered Third Gate, I fifgured I was to be sacraficed on the Altar of Innoruuk. Instead, I was taken to a building I had never ventured into before. In fact, I do not recall ever noticing it before that day. I was thrown on the floor at the feet of another man. There were five in the room ( I learned early on to take stock of the odds very quickly). He told me his name was Tani, and I now belonged to him. He threw a bag at me, and told me to go fetch him some Snake skins and fangs. When that task was complete, I would begin my training.

So, with my Blade and that bag, I ventured out into the Nektulos Forest. I fought off hungry wolves, and the walking dead in my hunt for the snakes I needed to complete my task. As I fought, I noticed that even though I could not hit them very hard, my aim was true, and my attacks were fast. I watched the Warriors, and Knights of Shadow nearby, I attacked three times for every two of their attacks. Thats when I began to see the strength in my weakness. I fought for many weeks in the forest, refining my skills with the Blade as well as the art of finding and attacking my prey undetected. I learned to make leather armor out of the wolves that I killed. and collected many coins and weapons from the dead.

Soon, it was no task at all for me to dispatch anything I met in the Nektulos Forest. Excluding the Halflings, I'd planned on visiting them later. I ventured forth into the East Commons. There, I meet the paleskins. Not knowing whether they were a threat or not, I decided to temporarily ally myself with them until I took stock of their abilities. We fought the Deathfist Orcs. During this time, I realized that while the Orcs were busy fighting, I could easily dip into their purses, and relieve them on uneeded coin. This is also where I learned that if I got behind my foe, I could strike him more accurately, hurting him worse than any sword blow.

The months rolled by, and I learned many things. I began fightin with two blades, for I found that I could strike even faster with two. Soon, I had learned all I could from fighting the Orcs, and moved on. I fought Bandits, and Giant spiders, and Willow Wisps. Learning the whole time. One day, I ventured to the Oasis of Marr. I had heard that the Reptiles that roamed the beach were quite a challenge. There I met Dajiba, a mighty Troll Warrior. Him and I roamed the beach, slaying everything in our path. It was a good deal, the gators bit him while he beat on their heads, and I slipped in behind them, and stabbed them as fast and hard as I could. Dajiba talked much of his family. He referred to them as The Bloodhorde. Wanting to learn all I could, I asked him about his family. I had rarely seen let alone met Trolls in Neriak. He spoke of his Warlord Zhokaii. It was then that I realized thet this was not his Blood family, but his adopted family. A Troll named Bakaa soon came to fight with us. I watched him closely, because he fought suspiciously like the Dragoons of Neriak. He could slay his victims with a mere touch of his hand if he desired. Then, a Tier'Dal female named Khadice came to fight with us. She fought like a Warrioress. When I learned that she too was adopted into The Bloodhorde, it piqued my interest. I asked them all how they came to be adopted by Zhokaii, and the Bloodhorde. They all said the same thing; They had proven their courage and dedication to Zhokaii in battle. So, I asked them if I could meet "The Warlord". They all laughed amongst themselves. I was insulted, enraged, and I hated them. Then, I was told that she already knew of me and that she was making the journey to appraise me.

When Zhokaii came to us, she was not alone. She brought with her a huge Ogre called Kolu. Kolu made me nervous, for she too was a Knight of Shadow. Not a bright one, but one none the less. Kolu never strayed far from Zhokaii. Zhokaii sat in silence for a long time. She peered at me with her one good eye, watching every move I made. It appeared to me that she was some sort of Witchdoctor, or Shaman.She asked me a few questions. Mostly pertaining to what God I worshipped, and what I thought I could bring to her family. I spoke candidly and true. I feared that if I lied to her, she would see through it....  even with one eye. Then, she said something that made me weak in the knees; "Voness, if joo wan to join Zhokaii's familee, joo must fite. Joo weel fite Bakaa or Dajiba, joo chuz." I had no doubt in my mind who I was going to fight. I headed towards Bakaa, and he grinned and readied his weapon, a gleam of Bloodlust in his eye. At the very last second, I attacked....  Dajiba. I knew better than to trifle with the Dark Knight. Dajiba's reflexes were quicker than I had hoped. I had only hit him once or twice before he started raining blows down on me form above. I ran around him, in circles, darting back and forth, hoping to keep him off balance, and hopefuly get behind him and strike a telling blow. As many blows as I avoided, it was not enough. I soon slumped to the sand, beaten and mangled. Hurting and bleeding. Dajiba laughing at me, all of them laughing at me. I hated them for it.

Zhokaii then said "Joo weel do." Then she chanted some unintelligable words, and made a few gestures, and my wounds healed right before my eyes and I found the strength to stand. Zhokaii then said "Frum now on, wen dey ask joo hoo joo ar, joo tell dem dat joo are Bloodhorde."

I have been Bloodhorde for many years now. I have killed, schemed, and conned my way to the top of the ranks. Hatred fueling my ambitions the whole way. I pity the fool who believes they will one day hold my position, for thier death will be quick and merciless and they will hate me for it.
  </td></tr>
